---
import ParadoxLayout from '../layouts/ParadoxLayout.astro';
---

<ParadoxLayout slug="jeane-dixon-effect">
    <p class="text-slate-600 mb-6">
        The Jeane Dixon Effect, named for a mid-20th-century American psychic whose occasional
        correct-sounding guesses were long remembered while her many misses faded from public
        memory, describes a general habit of mind: people (and the media covering them) tend to
        remember confirming "hits" much better than disconfirming "non-hits." The underlying
        prediction record never changes, but selective memory alone can make it look far more
        impressive in hindsight than it really was. Adjust the sliders below to see how big a gap
        selective memory can open up between an actual track record and the one people remember.
    </p>

    <div id="jde-explorer" class="jde-main-grid">
        <div class="jde-panel jde-controls">
            <div>
                <h3 class="jde-section-title">Change the underlying record</h3>
                <p class="jde-section-help">
                    These controls describe what actually happens before memory or reporting
                    enters the picture.
                </p>
            </div>

            <label class="jde-control">
                <div class="jde-control-row">
                    <span>Predictions / opportunities</span>
                    <strong id="jde-n-out">100</strong>
                </div>
                <input id="jde-n" type="range" min="20" max="500" step="10" value="100" class="w-full accent-cyan-600">
            </label>

            <label class="jde-control">
                <div class="jde-control-row">
                    <span>Actual hit rate</span>
                    <strong id="jde-hit-rate-out">11%</strong>
                </div>
                <input id="jde-hit-rate" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="11" class="w-full accent-cyan-600">
            </label>

            <div class="jde-divider-section">
                <h3 class="jde-section-title">Change the memory filter</h3>
                <p class="jde-section-help">
                    A hit and a non-hit need not have the same chance of being remembered,
                    repeated, or retold.
                </p>
            </div>

            <label class="jde-control">
                <div class="jde-control-row">
                    <span>Hits remembered</span>
                    <strong id="jde-hit-recall-out">60%</strong>
                </div>
                <input id="jde-hit-recall" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="60" class="w-full accent-cyan-600">
            </label>

            <label class="jde-control">
                <div class="jde-control-row">
                    <span>
                        Non-hits remembered
                        <sup>
                            <button type="button" class="jde-info-button jde-nonhit-info" aria-label="What does non-hit mean?">?</button>
                        </sup>
                    </span>
                    <strong id="jde-miss-recall-out">25%</strong>
                </div>
                <input id="jde-miss-recall" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="25" class="w-full accent-cyan-600">
            </label>

            <details class="jde-details">
                <summary>Optional: reinterpretation after the fact</summary>
                <p>
                    This is separate from selective memory. It represents remembered non-hits
                    later being reframed as hits because the original claim was broad or
                    flexible.
                </p>

                <label class="jde-control">
                    <div class="jde-control-row">
                        <span>Remembered non-hits reclassified as hits</span>
                        <strong id="jde-reinterpret-out">0%</strong>
                    </div>
                    <input id="jde-reinterpret" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="0" class="w-full accent-cyan-600">
                </label>
            </details>
        </div>

        <div class="jde-right-column">
            <div class="jde-panel jde-rate-panel">
                <div class="jde-rate-row">
                    <div class="jde-rate-block">
                        <div class="jde-rate-label">Actual success rate</div>
                        <div id="jde-actual-rate" class="jde-rate-value">11%</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="jde-rate-block jde-rate-block-right">
                        <div class="jde-rate-label">Apparent remembered rate</div>
                        <div id="jde-apparent-rate" class="jde-rate-value">23%</div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div id="jde-inflation-text" class="jde-inflation-text" aria-live="polite">
                    The remembered record makes an 11% hit rate look like 23%.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="jde-card jde-chart-card">
                <div>
                    <div class="jde-bar-heading">
                        <strong>What actually happened</strong>
                        <span id="jde-actual-counts" class="jde-counts">11 hits &middot; 89 non-hits</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="jde-stacked-bar" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of actual outcomes: 11% hits, 89% non-hits">
                        <div id="jde-actual-hit-bar" class="jde-bar-segment jde-bar-hits" style="width:11%">
                            <span id="jde-actual-hit-label">11%</span>
                        </div>
                        <div id="jde-actual-miss-bar" class="jde-bar-segment jde-bar-misses" style="width:89%">
                            <span id="jde-actual-miss-label">89%</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="jde-legend-row">
                        <span>Hits</span>
                        <span>
                            Non-hits
                            <sup>
                                <button type="button" class="jde-info-button jde-nonhit-info" aria-label="What does non-hit mean?">?</button>
                            </sup>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="jde-memory-divider">
                    <span>selective memory / reporting</span>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <div class="jde-bar-heading">
                        <strong>What remains in the remembered record</strong>
                        <span id="jde-remembered-counts" class="jde-counts">6.6 hits &middot; 22 non-hits</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="jde-stacked-bar" role="img" aria-label="Bar chart of remembered outcomes: 23% hits, 77% non-hits">
                        <div id="jde-remembered-hit-bar" class="jde-bar-segment jde-bar-hits" style="width:22.8769%">
                            <span id="jde-remembered-hit-label">23%</span>
                        </div>
                        <div id="jde-remembered-miss-bar" class="jde-bar-segment jde-bar-misses" style="width:77.1231%">
                            <span id="jde-remembered-miss-label">77%</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="jde-legend-row">
                        <span>Remembered as hits</span>
                        <span>
                            Remembered as non-hits
                            <sup>
                                <button type="button" class="jde-info-button jde-nonhit-info" aria-label="What does non-hit mean?">?</button>
                            </sup>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="jde-metrics">
                <div class="jde-metric-card">
                    <div id="jde-hits-survive" class="jde-metric-value">6.6</div>
                    <div class="jde-metric-label">hits surviving</div>
                </div>

                <div class="jde-metric-card">
                    <div id="jde-misses-survive" class="jde-metric-value">22</div>
                    <div class="jde-metric-label">non-hits surviving</div>
                </div>

                <div class="jde-metric-card">
                    <div id="jde-forgotten" class="jde-metric-value">71</div>
                    <div class="jde-metric-label">events forgotten</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="jde-explanation">
                <strong>What the visualization demonstrates</strong>
                <p>
                    The underlying hit rate never changes. Only the probability that hits and
                    non-hits survive into the remembered record changes. When hits are much more
                    memorable than non-hits, the apparent track record can become dramatically
                    better than the complete record.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <dialog id="jde-nonhit-dialog" class="jde-definition-dialog" aria-labelledby="jde-nonhit-dialog-title">
            <div class="jde-dialog-inner">
                <div class="jde-dialog-header">
                    <h3 id="jde-nonhit-dialog-title" class="jde-dialog-title">Why "non-hit" instead of "miss"?</h3>
                    <button id="jde-nonhit-dialog-close" type="button" class="jde-dialog-close" aria-label="Close explanation">&times;</button>
                </div>
                <div class="jde-dialog-body">
                    <p>
                        The large prediction audit used to anchor the default hit rate did not
                        classify every unsuccessful prediction as simply "wrong." Predictions
                        could also be too vague to score, obvious or expected, or impossible to
                        verify.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        In the Great Australian Psychic Prediction Project, the published
                        predictions were classified as:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="jde-dialog-breakdown">
                        <li><strong>11%</strong> correct</li>
                        <li><strong>53%</strong> wrong</li>
                        <li><strong>15%</strong> expected or obvious</li>
                        <li><strong>19%</strong> too vague</li>
                        <li><strong>2%</strong> unknown</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>
                        This visualization therefore uses <strong>non-hit</strong> for the other
                        89%: anything that did not qualify as a scored correct prediction. That
                        avoids incorrectly labeling vague, obvious, or uncheckable statements as
                        definite misses.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </dialog>

        <div class="jde-reset-row">
            <button id="jde-reset" type="button" class="jde-reset-button">Reset example</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-6">
        Further reading:
        <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeane_Dixon_effect" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-600 underline hover:text-cyan-800">Jeane Dixon effect on Wikipedia</a>
        &middot;
        <a href="https://www.skeptics.com.au/psychic-project-full-results-released/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-600 underline hover:text-cyan-800">The Great Australian Psychic Prediction Project</a>.
    </p>
</ParadoxLayout>

<style is:global>
    /*
     * Scoped-by-prefix styles for this exhibit only (jde-, following the
     * site's convention for exhibits whose layout is too specific for
     * Tailwind's utility classes alone -- see random-streaks.astro / rs- and
     * this-couldnt-be-coincidence.astro / tccbc- for the same pattern).
     * `is:global` matches how those exhibits' styles are declared; genuine
     * scoping comes from the jde- class prefix, not Astro's scoped-CSS
     * feature, since the section below is teleported into a <dialog> that
     * Astro's automatic scoping attribute does not reliably reach.
     *
     * This layout intentionally mirrors the original standalone HTML
     * prototype's structure closely (two-column controls/results grid,
     * stacked comparison bars, definition dialog) per explicit request, with
     * only the color palette changed to the site's own colorblind-safe
     * scheme. Colors are written as literal hex values with a Tailwind
     * color-name comment, matching this file's sibling exhibits.
     */

    .jde-main-grid {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1rem;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
        align-items: start;
    }

    .jde-panel,
    .jde-card {
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
    }

    .jde-panel {
        background: #f8fafc; /* slate-50 */
    }

    .jde-card {
        background: #ffffff;
    }

    .jde-controls {
        padding: 1rem;
    }

    .jde-right-column {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1rem;
        min-width: 0;
    }

    .jde-section-title {
        font-size: 1rem;
        font-weight: 650;
        line-height: 1.35;
        color: #1e293b; /* slate-800 */
    }

    .jde-section-help {
        margin-top: 0.25rem;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .jde-control {
        display: block;
        margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    .jde-control-row {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: baseline;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        color: #334155; /* slate-700 */
    }

    .jde-control-row strong {
        font-weight: 700;
        white-space: nowrap;
        color: #0f172a; /* slate-900 */
    }

    .jde-divider-section {
        margin-top: 1rem;
        padding-top: 1rem;
        border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
    }

    .jde-details {
        margin-top: 1rem;
        padding-top: 0.75rem;
        border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
    }

    .jde-details summary {
        cursor: pointer;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        color: #334155; /* slate-700 */
    }

    .jde-details p {
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .jde-info-button {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        width: 17px;
        height: 17px;
        margin-left: 2px;
        padding: 0;
        border: 1px solid #94a3b8; /* slate-400 */
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: transparent;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 11px;
        font-weight: 700;
        line-height: 1;
        vertical-align: super;
        cursor: pointer;
    }

    .jde-info-button:hover {
        border-color: #334155; /* slate-700 */
        color: #334155; /* slate-700 */
    }

    .jde-info-button:focus-visible,
    .jde-reset-button:focus-visible,
    .jde-dialog-close:focus-visible,
    .jde-main-grid input[type="range"]:focus-visible {
        outline: 2px solid #0891b2; /* cyan-600 */
        outline-offset: 2px;
    }

    .jde-rate-panel {
        padding: 1rem;
    }

    .jde-rate-row {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        align-items: baseline;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    }

    .jde-rate-label {
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 0.875rem;
    }

    .jde-rate-value {
        margin-top: 1px;
        font-size: 1.875rem;
        line-height: 1.1;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
        color: #0f172a; /* slate-900 */
    }

    .jde-rate-block-right {
        text-align: right;
    }

    .jde-inflation-text {
        margin-top: 0.75rem;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.45;
    }

    .jde-chart-card {
        padding: 1rem;
        display: grid;
        gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .jde-bar-heading {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        color: #334155; /* slate-700 */
    }

    .jde-counts {
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        text-align: right;
        white-space: nowrap;
    }

    .jde-stacked-bar {
        display: flex;
        height: 3rem;
        overflow: hidden;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        background: #f1f5f9; /* slate-100 */
    }

    .jde-bar-segment {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        min-width: 0;
        transition: width 140ms ease;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        font-weight: 650;
        color: #0f172a; /* slate-900 */
    }

    /*
     * Colorblind-safe hit/non-hit pair (from the "Wong" palette commonly
     * recommended for categorical data in vision-science guidance): blue
     * reads clearly against orange under all three common forms of color
     * vision deficiency (protanopia, deuteranopia, tritanopia), unlike the
     * green/gold pairing used in the original standalone prototype this
     * exhibit was ported from. Adjacent text labels and the legend below
     * each bar also carry the meaning, so the distinction never depends on
     * color alone.
     */
    .jde-bar-hits {
        background: #0072b2;
        color: #ffffff;
    }

    .jde-bar-misses {
        background: #e69f00;
        color: #0f172a; /* slate-900, for contrast against the lighter orange */
    }

    .jde-legend-row {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        margin-top: 0.5rem;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 0.75rem;
    }

    .jde-memory-divider {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 0.875rem;
    }

    .jde-memory-divider::before,
    .jde-memory-divider::after {
        content: "";
        height: 1px;
        flex: 1;
        background: #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
    }

    .jde-metrics {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 0.5rem;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .jde-metric-card {
        padding: 0.75rem;
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
        background: #ffffff;
    }

    .jde-metric-value {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #0f172a; /* slate-900 */
    }

    .jde-metric-label {
        margin-top: 0.125rem;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        line-height: 1.35;
    }

    .jde-explanation {
        padding: 1rem;
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
        background: #ffffff;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        color: #334155; /* slate-700 */
    }

    .jde-explanation p {
        margin-top: 0.25rem;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .jde-definition-dialog {
        /* Explicit fixed-position centering rather than relying on the
           <dialog> UA stylesheet's default margin:auto centering, which is
           unreliable when the dialog is nested inside a CSS Grid container
           (as it is here, inside .jde-main-grid) -- some browsers fail to
           center it in that case and it renders pinned to the top-left. */
        position: fixed;
        top: 50%;
        left: 50%;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
        margin: 0;
        width: min(520px, calc(100% - 2rem));
        max-height: calc(100% - 2rem);
        padding: 0;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        background: #ffffff;
        color: #1e293b; /* slate-800 */
        box-shadow: 0 18px 55px rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.20);
    }

    .jde-definition-dialog::backdrop {
        background: rgba(17, 24, 39, 0.45);
    }

    .jde-dialog-inner {
        padding: 1.25rem;
    }

    .jde-dialog-header {
        display: flex;
        align-items: flex-start;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 1rem;
    }

    .jde-dialog-title {
        font-size: 1.125rem;
        line-height: 1.3;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #0f172a; /* slate-900 */
    }

    .jde-dialog-close {
        flex: 0 0 auto;
        width: 36px;
        height: 36px;
        padding: 0;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; /* slate-200 */
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        background: transparent;
        color: #1e293b; /* slate-800 */
        font-size: 22px;
        line-height: 1;
        cursor: pointer;
    }

    .jde-dialog-close:hover {
        background: #f8fafc; /* slate-50 */
    }

    .jde-dialog-body {
        margin-top: 0.75rem;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .jde-dialog-body p + p {
        margin-top: 0.625rem;
    }

    .jde-dialog-breakdown {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
        list-style: disc;
        color: #64748b; /* slate-500 */
    }

    .jde-dialog-breakdown li + li {
        margin-top: 0.25rem;
    }

    .jde-reset-row {
        margin-top: 1.25rem;
    }

    .jde-reset-button {
        min-height: 44px;
        padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
        border: 1px solid #cbd5e1; /* slate-300 */
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        background: transparent;
        color: #1e293b; /* slate-800 */
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        cursor: pointer;
    }

    .jde-reset-button:hover {
        background: #f8fafc; /* slate-50 */
    }

    @media (max-width: 680px) {
        .jde-main-grid {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .jde-rate-block-right {
            text-align: left;
        }

        .jde-rate-row {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        }

        .jde-bar-heading {
            display: block;
        }

        .jde-counts {
            margin-top: 0.125rem;
            text-align: left;
            white-space: normal;
        }
    }

    @media (max-width: 420px) {
        .jde-rate-row {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .jde-metrics {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .jde-legend-row {
            align-items: flex-start;
        }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .jde-bar-segment {
            transition: none;
        }
    }
</style>

<script>
    import '../scripts/paradoxes/jeane-dixon-effect.js';
</script>
